+(defn segments
+  "A reply's forms (`:reply`, the default: prose becomes comments) or code's.
+
+  Code (`:code`) is read as written: every form is a form, nothing is
+  repaired. A reply holding a Markdown fence runs only its Clojure fences'
+  forms, every one of them (`fenced`). Reading is structural (edamame, every
+  semantic hook neutral: tags unread, any alias), with the forgiving stage's
+  repairs: each form's source text and the prose above it as its comment. A
+  balanced form the structural read refuses (an odd map) is one form whose
+  evaluation-time read answers its error once, and reading continues after
+  it; an unbalanced rest is the unread rest. The one semantic read of each
+  form happens later, at the live cursor, when it is evaluated."
+  {:malli/schema [:function
+                  [:=> [:cat :string] :seon.batch/segmented]
+                  [:=> [:cat :string :seon.batch/mode] :seon.batch/segmented]]}
+  ([text] (segments text :reply))
+  ([text mode]
+   (if-let [markdown (when (= :reply mode) (fenced text))]
+     (read-segments markdown :fenced)
+     (read-segments text mode))))
